  "story": "Parcels leave the warehouse on a conveyor in a fixed order, each with a whole-number weight. A single cart carries them away in trips. On each trip the cart takes the next parcels in line for as long as their total weight fits its capacity, then leaves; parcels are never reordered or split. You may make at most the given number of trips. What is the smallest whole-number capacity that clears the whole conveyor in time?",
  "io": {
    "inputs": [
      {"name": "weights", "type": "array<num>"},
      {"name": "trips", "type": "num"}
    ],
    "output": {"type": "num"}
  },
  "constraints": {
    "n": {"min": 1, "max": 300},
    "notes": ["Weights are whole numbers from 1 to 500.", "Trips is a whole number from 1 to the number of parcels."]
  },
